Consider the two functions incr and decr shown below. 
<pre><code>
incr(){
  wait(s);
  X = X+1;
  signal(s);
}

decr(){
  wait(s);
  X = X-1;
  signal(s);
}

</pre></code>There are 5 threads each invoking incr once, and 3 threads each invoking decr
once, on the same shared variable X. The initial value of X is 10.<br>
Suppose there are two implementations of the semaphore [latex]s[/latex], as follows:<br><br>
I-1: s is a binary semaphore initialized to 1.
<br>I-2: s is a counting semaphore initialized to 2.
<br><br>Let V1, V2 be the values of X at the end of execution of all the threads with
implementations I-1, I-2, respectively.<br>
Which one of the following choices corresponds to the minimum possible values of
V1, V2, respectively?
